<<<
fitnessis all. An allusion that strikes

a light in one company will only

darken counsel in another; most

audiences are acquainted with the

qualities of a Samson, fewer with

those of a Dominie Sampson, fewer still with those of the Laputans, &
===
fitness is all. An allusion that strikes a light in one company will only darken counsel in another; most audiences are acquainted with the qualities of *a Samson*, fewer with those of *a Dominie Sampson*, fewer still with those of *the Laputans*, &
>>>

<<<
*the Laputans*, &

yet fewer again with those of Lihuriel’s spear.
===
*the Laputans*, & yet fewer again with those of *Ithuriel's spear*.
>>>

<<<
they will not like it, nor him,
===
they will not like it, nor him.
>>>

<<<
genie. Pronounce jé’ni; pl. genii, pron. jé‘nii; see LATIN PLURALS. Another form is jinnee, pl. jinn.
===
**genie.** Pronounce jē'nĭ; pl. *genii*, pron. jē'nĭī; see ^^LATIN PLURALS^^. Another form is *jinnee*, pl. *jinn*.
>>>

<<<
genitive(ly), genitival(ly). See AB- LATIVELY.
===
**genitive(ly), genitival(ly).** See ^^ABLATIVELY^^.
>>>

<<<
genius. Pl. -uses; the form genii is now used only as pl. of genie (or of genius in the sense of genie); see LATIN PLURALS. For g. & talent, see TALENT.
===
**genius.** Pl. *-uses*; the form *genii* is now used only as pl. of *genie* (or of *genius* in the sense of *genie*); see ^^LATIN PLURALS^^. For g. & talent, see ^^TALENT^^.
>>>

<<<
genre. See FRENCH WORDS.
===
**genre.** See ^^FRENCH WORDS^^.
>>>

<<<
gens. Pl. gentes, pron. -éz.
===
**gens.** Pl. *gentes*, pron. -ēz.
>>>

<<<
gent ( = gentleman) is used only in uneducated speech or in jocular imitations of it.
===
**gent** ( = gentleman) is used only in uneducated speech or in jocular imitations of it.
>>>

<<<
genteel is now used, except by the ignorant, only in mockery.
===
**genteel** is now used, except by the ignorant, only in mockery.
>>>

<<<
genteelly. So spelt.
===
**genteelly.** So spelt.
>>>

<<<
GENTEELISM. By gentcelism is here
===
**GENTEELISM.** By *genteelism* is here
>>>

<<<
The truly genteel do not offer beer, but ale; invite one to step, not come, this way; take in not lodgers, but paying guests;
===
The truly genteel do not offer *beer*, but *ale*; invite one to *step*, not *come*, this way; take in not *lodgers*, but *paying guests*;
>>>

<<<
send their boys not to school, but to college; never help, but assist, each other to potatoes;
===
send their boys not to *school*, but to *college*; never *help*, but *assist*, each other to potatoes;
>>>

<<<
keep stomachs & domestics instead of bellies & servants; & have quite forgotten
===
keep *stomachs* & *domestics* instead of *bellies* & *servants*; & have quite forgotten
>>>

<<<
guilty of toothpowder & napkins & underclothing, of before & except & about, where nothing now will do for them but dentifrice, serviette, lingerie, ere, save, anent.
===
guilty of *toothpowder* & *napkins* & *underclothing*, of *before* & *except* & *about*, where nothing now will do for them but *dentifrice, serviette, lingerie, ere, save, anent*.
>>>

